  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Beginning cash = beginning fund balances 5,287,439 (p4), ending = 3,265,703 (p4 and p3). Governmental funds only; no business-type funds. 'Taxes' (2,577,469) split into property/motor vehicle/lodging using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2). Local 751,752 and Intergovernmental are broad groups (no state aid breakdown printed). Other financing = insurance proceeds 20,852 + sale of surplus 48,467. Transfers in = out = 1,200,937 (balanced). Transfer cross-check: General Fund out 1,156,704 = Road 414,971 + Highway Buyback 728,170 + ARP 6,647 + nonmajor 6,916; General in 44,233 = nonmajor outflows 39,809 + 4,424; all transfers are shown as transfers, not in spending. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) recorded for departments; its Actual receipts (3,718,831) differ from the General Fund combining statement (p5, 3,688,320 for the General sub-fund + 447,342 inheritance) because the budget schedule includes insurance proceeds and sale of surplus in Local and excludes the Inheritance Tax sub-fund; the p5 General Fund combining statement is not otherwise duplicated, only the Inheritance Tax sub-fund lines are added. Road Fund budget schedule Local 58,848 includes sale of surplus 38,808. Nonmajor funds recorded with the combined total column (p7) since there are 10 funds. Highway Buyback budget schedule shows ending change 705,135 in the 'receipts under disbursements and other financing' Actual line (printed as is). Audit recheck 2026-10-22: General Fund budget Taxes split into property/motor vehicle per p2; budget-schedule Local lines split into Local + insurance proceeds/sale of surplus per p4 (budget amounts kept on the Local item). Re-check 2026-10-28 (attempt 2): balance sheet now from the Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p3), Total Governmental Funds column, whose totals (3,265,703) equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); fund balance by classification (9 Restricted, Committed road maintenance 155,546, Unassigned 2,165,439). Read pages 1-11 of 11."
